tain South Bank Exhibition.","date":"1951","hidden":"true","publicdate":"2005-10-07 10:45:15","addeddate":"2005-10-07 17:44:35","uploader":"florian@archive.org","sponsor":"Central Office of Information for Commonwealth Relations Office","director":"Phillip Leacock","publisher":"Crown Film Unit","sound":"sound","color":"color","runtime":"9:31","credits":"Public Information Films","rights":"UK Crown Copyright","language":"english","coverage":"Great Britain","updatedate":"2005-10-07 10:46:51","updater":"nVIR","backup_location":"ia903600_10","ia_orig__runtime":"9 Minutes 31 Seconds"},"reviews":[{"reviewbody":"A somewhat livelier, thank heavens!, snapshot of the London fair here. But once again, the filmmakers seem to focus on how educational, how you know, BRITISH the whole thing was, the first half doesnt go beyond the fair being one big museum exhibit. Hardly anyone is looking to be having fun, like it was one big government glorification (which it [probably was, come to think of it). Display after mind numbing display is shown. It's not til the final third when we realize that the British have some sort of fun in them as we go to the festival's midway! The fair is PACKED, which should speak volume of what the fair should have accomplished (but failed)","reviewtitle":"Startling political commentary by me follows!","reviewer":"Spuzz","reviewdate":"2008-05-26 20:32:09","createdate":"2008-05-26 20:32:09","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"My guess is that the reviewer Spuzz is very young, and certainly didn't live through the years immediately after the Second World War.  If he thinks that the Festival of Britain wasn't fun, he's just too far away from the event to have any real idea of it.\n\nI attended the Festival of Britain when I was 8 years old, and some of the things I saw remain with me to this day.\n\nIt was the most wonderful and exciting day out for my and my younger brother, although we weren't old enough to understand all the exhibits.","reviewtitle":"What it was like at the Festival of Britain","reviewer":"Sashalu","reviewdate":"2009-04-01 14:33:33","createdate":"2009-04-01 14:33:33","stars":"5"},{"reviewbody":"Being before my time, this was okay to watch but wished the commentator would have more effort to describe what I was seeing and why it was important to Britons.\nI can understand why it was fun for the previous reviewers to reminisce over, though.","reviewtitle":"a little underwhelmed","reviewer":"Gopher_Baroque","reviewdate":"2010-01-01 04:30:18","createdate":"2010-01-01 04:30:18","stars":"2"},{"reviewbody":"MY RELATION WENT THERE - AS A CHILD - ALLEGEDLY. I KNEW THIS TO BE THE CASE THAT SHE'D GONE WALKABOUT IN LONDON... HAD PREMONITION AS I ALSO WALKED ABOUT A BIT THAT SHE'D BEEN WANDRIN' ABOUT BARBICAN AREA AS SOMEONE GOT ANGRY COS THEY COULDN'T LOCATE SOUTHBANK... SUCH WAS THAT NARCOLEPSY YOU INDUCED.\nPITY BRITAIN DOESN'T FEEL ITSELF WORTHY OF DOINGSOMETHING AKIN TO THIS AGAIN - HAVING ITS WORDLY FRIENDS PUT ON STALLS AND EXHIBIT ITS WARES AND/OR CULTURAL FORMATS... BEREFTOF JINGOISM IT'D BE COOL... THOUGH I DOUBT YOU COULD ACHIEVE THAT WITHOUT THOSE BUMBLING PATRIOTS.","reviewtitle":"TOTAL DISCOVERY... MAN'S INTERMISSION...","reviewer":"NOTVERYHIP.INC","reviewer_itemname":"@notveryhip_inc","reviewdate":"2019-08-14 11:24:58","createdate":"2019-08-14 11:24:58","stars":"5"}],"server":"dn800206.us.archive.org","simplelists":{"solo_manifest":{"solo_manifest_dn800206":{"sys_changed_by":{"source":"task","task_id":"5408474595"},"sys_last_changed":"2026-06-01 12:06:26.780143"}}},"solo":true,"uniq":789893681,"workable_servers":["dn800206.us.archive.org"]}